cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mentori or the evaluation methodology in your own work, please cite both the paper and this software."
type: software
title: "Mentori: a locally-hosted agentic AI workspace for scientists"
abstract: >-
  Mentori is a multi-agent AI workspace that combines a chat interface,
  retrieval-augmented document analysis, and a Jupyter-based code execution
  sandbox. This repository accompanies the paper "Systematic ablation of
  multiagent artificial intelligence for the life sciences" (Bianchi &
  Schokker, submitted to Communications AI & Computing), which applies a
  triple-triangulation evaluation methodology for retrieval-augmented
  multi-agent systems to more than 50,000 individual evaluations spanning
  200 scientific papers and 250 expert-curated questions.
